      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Although carpal tunnel syndrome (CTS) is a common entrapment neuropathy, reflex sympathetic dystrophy is an extremely rare and devastating complication. In this report, a case of chemical sympathectomy in a patient who had undergone previous three surgical interventions elsewhere for unilateral CTS, with persistent sympathetic pain."},
